# Coucou is built on Windows, macOS and Linux from one checkout, and this
# repository is worked on from all three. A CRLF line ending in a shell script
# or a .desktop file is not a cosmetic difference: `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` is
# "no such file or directory" on Linux, and desktop-file-validate rejects the
# entry. Text stays LF everywhere; only files that are genuinely binary are
# left to Git's own detection.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ttf binary
*.xcassets binary

